<p>British counterterrorism police are investigating whether a recent series of arson attacks on Jewish sites in London was carried out by proxies linked to Iran. The latest fire caused minor damage Saturday night, and authorities said no one was injured in any of the blazes reported so far. Police are treating the incidents as possible terrorism-related offenses. They are also examining online claims of responsibility and other evidence that could show whether the attacks were coordinated.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/9u1UM1E94b9aGXqThV7g9k-yaNNt4HlcPvFb76-5_MIIM9rex7aRPO-L9dqHKB3DWPiJWoQ4X96gzq6PE1p3-DVufg1OxilTld5QdfdOt4Nk0uEMbl4luNgvB1IVekaZWAvVimfzMXu30kzwrJnn-LuzyOtyn-0wzOe0XQUhDF3fBNXt7hx1i1NW5HD1DGmgo7BDmA' alt='Police forensic officers worked Sunday inside a cordon set up near Kenton United Synagogue. The synagogue, in Harrow, northwest London, was the scene of an overnight arson attack.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Claimed responsibility: Coverage said HAYI claimed responsibility on Telegram, giving investigators a clear online trail as they assess whether the group has any real operational link to Iran.</li><li>North London firebombing: One reported incident targeted a synagogue in North London in what coverage described as a firebombing attack and a suspected act of terrorism, underscoring why specialists are leading the case.</li><li>Media target: Authorities are also investigating an attack on a Persian-language media company, widening the inquiry beyond Jewish communal institutions and suggesting the targets may have been chosen to intimidate multiple communities.</li></ul><blockquote>British Jews are facing a campaign of violence and intimidation - Chief Rabbi Ephraim Mirvis</blockquote><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/20/g-s1-118083/police-investigating-london-iranian-proxies'>U.K police investigating if attacks in London are the work of Iranian proxies</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.co